      "content": "It's reassuring to hear that the discomfort is only mildly bothersome, and it's wise to consider cost-effective options. Taking ibuprofen and antacids may provide relief, but it's important to monitor the pain and check for any signs of worsening, such as fever, vomiting, jaundice (yellowing of the skin or eyes), or changes in urine color, among others. Additionally, keep an eye on the location and nature of the pain. If the discomfort intensifies, becomes sharp, spreads drastically, or is accompanied by any of the above symptoms, you should seek medical attention promptly, even if you're trying to avoid an ER visit unless it's an emergency. Staying hydrated and avoiding large meals can also help manage symptoms. Take it easy and give your body time to settle. If you remain concerned, not rushing to the ER often allows for an accurate assessment, but never hesitate to seek help if your condition deteriorates.",
